(6874165, 1035427, 108580, '<td valign="top">Mesmerising and the use of the long exposure quite literally "sucks the viewer in". <br/>Unique image, not that it hasn''t been used before :) but you are the only one on DPC I think that has Giles. Great TOD to take the shot with distant lights and some activity in the sky. Long exposure has mirrored the lake. It just seems overall a tad dark: the hills and the ''portal'' specifically. <br/>It''s such a difficult decision to make; should you leave it as you shot it or should you boost the contrast and saturation for a FS? 7.</td>', 'Mesmerising and the use of the long exposure quite literally "sucks the viewer in". Unique image, not that it hasn''t been used before :) but you are the only one on DPC I think that has Giles. Great TOD to take the shot with distant lights and some activity in the sky. Long exposure has mirrored the lake. It just seems overall a tad dark: the hills and the ''portal'' specifically. It''s such a difficult decision to make; should you leave it as you shot it or should you boost the contrast and saturation for a FS? 7.', '2012-10-03 03:20:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6874167, 1034781, 108580, '<td valign="top">Every now and then something unique pops up on DPC. This is it. Has that romantic ye olde feel to it. The slight mist or haze in the BG has helped in making subjects pop. So has the red dress! Look forward to the story behind the shot.</td>', 'Every now and then something unique pops up on DPC. This is it. Has that romantic ye olde feel to it. The slight mist or haze in the BG has helped in making subjects pop. So has the red dress! Look forward to the story behind the shot.', '2012-10-03 03:23:58.000000', NULL, 1),
